      "id": 7186,
      "name": "XChylde",
      "username": "XChylde",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/xchylde/{size}/2559_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-02-09T20:58:18.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>For several villians there are mechanics that make the first turn confusing.</p><p>1) Omnitron: He is setup factory side up. &nbsp;Does he flip to rampaging robot on his first turn immediately or would that happen on subsequent turns? &nbsp;My inclination would be to do exactly what it says and flip immediately. &nbsp;This also makes thematic sense since he has just become self aware and goes berserk.</p><p>2) Citizen Dawn: She has several citizens in play as part of her setup based on the number of heroes. &nbsp;Does she still play another card on her first turn or is the the setup her first card play phase? &nbsp;Again, my inclination is to simply have the standard villian play phase meaning she would in fact on round 1 also play another card beside what was setup.</p><p>3) Grand Warlord Voss: The same as above for Citizen Dawn.</p><p>I guess the ultimate question is, do villians still take there standard turn even after setup on the initial round?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:37:23.917Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
